==============================================================================
  5. what this does NOT say
==============================================================================
  * No whole-step number is a denominator anywhere above. The
    reference's whole step is printed as CONTEXT only: it is 7
    launches, five of them state updates.
  * The ratio against the reference is render-against-render, both
    producing the same uint8 observation at the same batch on the
    same card. If the digests differ, the ratio is between two
    different computations.
  * The clean-vs-faithful delta is the crossing cost. It is the only
    number here that no other arm in this study has.
  * Every ms above is DEVICE time: the sum of the per-kernel device
    times in the graph, measured with tinygrad's own time_call, host
    tracing excluded. The host build+realize number printed beside it
    is context and is NOT comparable to the reference's, because the
    reference pays no tracing cost. Calling realize() on an already
    realized tensor is a no-op; time_graph raises if handed one,
    because an earlier version of this file did exactly that and
    reported the port as 13x FASTER than the hand-written CUDA.

